Usage: chcon [OPTION]... CONTEXT FILE...
  or:  chcon [OPTION]... [-u USER] [-r ROLE] [-l RANGE] [-t TYPE] FILE...
  or:  chcon [OPTION]... --reference=RFILE FILE...

Change the SELinux security context of each FILE.

WinuxCmd accepts the GNU-compatible command line surface for chcon, but
Windows does not provide SELinux file contexts. This command therefore
acts as a compatibility command and reports that the operation is not
supported on Windows.

OPTIONS:
      --dereference       affect the referent of each symbolic link
  -h, --no-dereference    affect symbolic links instead of referenced files
      --preserve-root     fail to operate recursively on '/'
      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially
      --reference ARG     use RFILE's security context
  -u, --user ARG          set user component of the security context
  -r, --role ARG          set role component of the security context
  -t, --type ARG          set type component of the security context
  -l, --range ARG         set range component of the security context
  -R, --recursive         operate on files and directories recursively
  -H                      follow command-line symbolic links to directories
  -L                      follow every symbolic link to a directory
  -P                      do not follow symbolic links
  -v, --verbose           output a diagnostic for every file processed
      --help              display this help and exit
  -V, --version           output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
